  "final_message": "Trace of `service.checkout(\"7781\")`:\n\n1. `service.py:6` \u2014 `checkout` calls `write_audit(\"order\", order_id)` with `order_id = \"7781\"`.\n2. `audit.py:9-12` \u2014 `write_audit` builds the key via `_format_key(kind, ident)` and sets `log[key] = True`.\n3. `audit.py:5-6` \u2014 `_format_key` returns `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`.\n4. `config.py:3` \u2014 `AUDIT_PREFIX = \"AUD\"`; `\"order\".upper()` \u2192 `\"ORDER\"`.\n\nResult: `\"AUD\" + \"-\" + \"ORDER\" + \"-\" + \"7781\"`. Running the actual code confirms the log dict contains exactly one key, `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nThe decoy files are irrelevant: `decoy_metrics.py` uses `METRICS_PREFIX = \"MET\"` and writes to a separate metrics dict (never called by `service.py`), and `decoy_cache.py` never touches the audit log.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
